  "scope": {
    "rust": "Verus proves actual generic Pending<T> start/record_sync/needs_sync: exact description preservation, unknown initial state, monotonic confirmation from reported success and sync required when success is not known. Option assignment order, identity/path/descriptor mapping, I/O response classification, actual syscall/validation ordering and whole recovery remain unproved.",
    "tla": "Nine finite positive, four algorithm-negative and one environment-negative configuration. Starts after complete framing and open registration. Failed sync may persist; corruption must be rejected even after known success. Checks one completed file, fencing and durable verified returns. Progress requires fair retries/eventual stable modeled operations and may settle with corruption error. Negative cases select TypeOK plus the named consequence. Missing-path/rename progress, process restart, failures before complete framing and final catalog/GC handoff are not composed.",
    "four_host": "Three standalone APIs, 2 KiB/8 MiB repeated-byte source records, private independent pools. A shim skips one real fsync with EIO or returns EIO after actual success; a callback separately fails after straw has received success. Traces use private local /tmp files. No service crash, actual power loss, natural fault-rate or cross-host same-pool guarantee.",
    "measurement": "Old 72/72 cases rewrite a complete extent and leave an original partial; new 360/360 reuse the original file with zero retry payload chunks and complete read/release/GC. Extent byte counts are logical file sizes corroborated by retry payload callbacks, not physical-device traffic. Record_set retries its manifest, with source data prepared before timing. Input hashing/full checksum scans remain proportional to size.",
    "limits": "Groups n=4 old and n=20 new, nearest-rank p99 equals sample maximum; retries include hashing/authentication/catalog/barriers/tracing. No cache eviction or controlled background load, no delay bound, no new admission cap and no 100 GB/TB rerun. The preceding 100 GB evidence belongs to another binary. Historical orphan partials/open entries are not automatically repaired; same-writer recovery does not imply global or cross-process idempotency."
  },
